{"title":"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nI have an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> sheet of stamps, from which I've been asked to tear out blocks of three adjacent stamps in a single row or column. (I can only tear along the perforations separating adjacent stamps, and each block must come out of the sheet in one piece.) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> be the smallest number of blocks I can tear out and make it impossible to tear out any more blocks. Prove that there are real constants <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f8227e8e6f5e87f8ff9762baf0e1f00748cd32eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{7} n^2 - cn \\leq b(n) \\leq \\dfrac{1}{5} n^2 + dn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"227\" height=\"37\" /></center><p> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1431ad346632b25a0e7b3f12ebe19723b3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The upper bound requires an example of a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84119c2626dea7591bf98c40b7fadec5f3f7a4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}n^2 + dn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" /> blocks whose removal makes it impossible to remove any further blocks. It suffices to show that we can tile the plane by tiles containing one block for every five stamps such that no more blocks can be chosen. Two such tilings are shown below with one tile outlined in heavy lines. Given an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> section of the tiling take all blocks lying entirely within that section and add as many additional blocks as possible. If the basic tile is contained in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de479eda262719ca41b570577d6c00314180521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m + 1)\\times (m + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> square, then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> section is covered by tiles contained in a concentric <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/564812b955e39372283eb6cc555b32374217cc4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 2m)\\times (n + 2m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" /> square. Hence there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab1e0a5749ca00415ad43dc738a8e54ea4494fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}(n + 2m)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" /> blocks entirely within the section. For an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> section of the tiling, there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b417a127620d5b467fe7a48ad5f7d843e5c390b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> blocks which lie partially in and partially out of that section (hence these blocks contain at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88f825e8eca022f48ac1d2d41cd80ad6e5d9ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> stamps in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> square) and each of the additional blocks must contain one of these stamps. Thus there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88f825e8eca022f48ac1d2d41cd80ad6e5d9ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> additional blocks. Thus there are at most\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba9fcacdfed8a8e3bf28b1e40b2ca62d0a7a649.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{5}(n + 2m)^2 + 8n\\leq \\frac{1}{5}n^2 + \\frac{4m^2 + 4m + 40}{5}n\\]\" width=\"345\" height=\"39\" />\nblocks total.\n</p>\n<center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2002usamo6-1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/50/2002usamo6-1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"589\" height=\"259\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<p>The lower bound requires an argument. Suppose that we have a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> blocks whose removal makes removing any further blocks impossible. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6c8285701ae24016d78c085d84916e129170a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n(n - 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> potential blocks of three consecutive stamps in a row or column. Each of these must meet at least one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> blocks removed. Conversely, each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> blocks removed meets at most 14 of these potential blocks (5 oriented the same way, including itself, and 9 oriented the orthogonal way). Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd945b680d2a5c53153b9cc272ad9163b230250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14b(n)\\geq 2n(n - 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" /> or\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782dfd839a21d77dc486e6a7114c2194a43531c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b(n)\\geq\\frac{1}{7}n^2 - \\frac{2}{7}n.\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Call a stamp used if it belongs to one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> removed blocks. Consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cad91b8f76fec35de44795b4e4204abc02da22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n - 2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> five-stamp crosses centered at each stamp not on an edge of the sheet. Each cross must contain two used stamps. (One stamp not in the center is not enough to prevent another block from being torn out, and it is impossible to use one stamp in the center and use no other stamps in the cross.) In addition, each block not lying along an edge of the sheet lies entirely inside one cross, which thus contains three used stamps. There are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a724e173ceccf20d8488f6afb3090d5eb17e9186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> blocks lying along the edges, hence there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd3c5c0e7dc20f4fba98a6879fde08237aa77d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n) - 4n/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> crosses containing three used stamps.\n</p><p>Now count the number of pairs of a used stamp and a cross containing that stamp, in two ways. First counting block by block, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65a9af850fcbf2cfc658627e70ade031c7f13d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> used stamps, and each used stamp is contained in at most five crosses (exactly five if it is not on an edge), for a total of at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30ed33a4c266f8200f785ffaf5941aad60d220ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> pairs. Next, counting cross by cross, each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cad91b8f76fec35de44795b4e4204abc02da22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n - 2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> crosses contains at least two used stamps and we have at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd3c5c0e7dc20f4fba98a6879fde08237aa77d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n) - 4n/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> crosses containing three used stamps, for a total of at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40d2a42a489523fc29608a79ad3d2f542464fc5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(n - 2)^2 + b(n) - 4n/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"19\" /> pairs. Therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb3f66f5f4bb818adfcc092cd9b33486443224e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[15b(n)\\geq 2(n - 2)^2 + b(n) - \\frac{4n}{3},\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"37\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd4acb48253b278a376c28799db0f7df20db74b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b(n)\\geq\\frac{1}{7}n^2 - \\frac{16}{21}n.\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Call a stamp used if it belongs to one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> removed blocks. Count the number of pairs consisting of a used stamp and an adjacent unused stamp, in two ways.\n</p><p>There are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1ca0845bb04db1950b8fd4c5c4e31898422336ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n - 2)^2 - 3b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"19\" /> unused stamps which are not on an edge. Since no more blocks can be torn out, either the stamp to the left or right and either the stamp or below such an unused stamp must be used. Thus we have at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/51276c945f6df9f9f3c87a12d7a62b125d633852.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n^2 - 8n - 6b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" /> such pairs.\n</p><p>Each block removed is adjacent to at most eight other stamps. However these eight stamps contain two blocks of three consecutive stamps. Hence at most six of these eight stamps can be unused. Thus each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36984855c12e2794ac302bfa57a05d47e7c1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> blocks removed is involved in at most six pairs. Thus there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f73315a19c657f7658a7ebbe5d1f768bfb107be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6b(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> pairs.\n</p><p>Combining these we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d6dec3d3751e1c1b53de6b4eb7e7e2a51943db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6b(n)\\geq 2n^2 - 8n - 6b(n),\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"19\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55cdde3198ba1c5b99859e48f31e70ae1139621c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b(n)\\geq\\frac{1}{6}n^2 - \\frac{2}{3}n.\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO\" title=\"2002 USAMO\">2002 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201219\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 272/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1633/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7763/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.145      1 -total\n 36.07%    6.545      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 33.66%    6.107      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 28.83%    5.231      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7429:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201219 and revision id 62523. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}